    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5343" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bīlĭōsus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		bilis. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of bile</i>, <i>bilious</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alvus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 2,
					8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sputum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 2,
				6</span></i>
			' biliosa reicere, <i><span class="en">Scrib. 168</span></i>.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bīlĭō-sus</span></b> ,
			i, m., <i>a bilious
			person</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 1, 3</span></i>.— <b>Trop.</b>, <i>hypochondriac</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">biliosus, quod sit semper tristis, ab umore
					nigro, qui bilis vocatur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 10, 30</span></i>
			.</div>
